    {q:"According to the levels-of-processing framework, which encoding is most likely to support durable recall?",a:"Semantic encoding that connects meaning to prior knowledge, rather than focusing only on appearance or sound.",d:["Rote rehearsal of visual features without considering meaning.","Briefly repeating a sound while preventing elaboration or retrieval.","Encoding an item only through its font, color, or spatial position."]},
    {q:"What does proactive interference predict in a memory task?",a:"Older learning makes it harder to retrieve newer, similar information.",d:["New learning makes it harder to retrieve older, similar information.","Emotional arousal always improves recall accuracy for every detail.","Retrieval practice weakens a memory more than passive rereading does."]},
    {q:"Why can a double-blind procedure reduce bias in a clinical study?",a:"It limits expectancy effects by keeping both participants and relevant researchers unaware of condition assignment.",d:["It guarantees random sampling from the entire population.","It prevents placebo effects by withholding treatment from every participant.","It removes measurement error by increasing the sample mean."]}
