    {q:"What is a key distinction between prejudice and discrimination?",a:"Prejudice is an attitude or belief; discrimination is differential treatment or action toward a group.",d:["Prejudice is institutional action, while discrimination is always a private belief.","They are identical terms and differ only by legal context.","Discrimination is a personality trait that cannot be observed in behavior."]}
