    ["What does an orthogonal projection do?","It maps a vector to its closest vector in a subspace under the Euclidean inner product."],
    ["Why are eigenvectors associated with distinct eigenvalues linearly independent?","A standard theorem for linear operators implies eigenvectors corresponding to distinct eigenvalues are independent."],
    ["What characterizes a symmetric real matrix's eigenvalues and eigenvectors?","Its eigenvalues are real and it has an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors."],
    ["What does the null space of a matrix contain?","All vectors mapped to the zero vector by that matrix."],
    ["How does a change-of-basis matrix work?","It converts coordinate representations of vectors between two bases of the same vector space."],
    ["What is the geometric meaning of an orthonormal basis?","Its basis vectors are mutually perpendicular unit vectors, simplifying coordinates and inner products."],
    ["When is a system Ax = b consistent?","When b lies in the column space of A, equivalently when it can be formed as a linear combination of A's columns."],
    ["What does diagonalization express for a matrix A?","When possible, it writes A as PDP⁻¹, representing the transformation in an eigenvector basis."],
    ["What is the trace of a square matrix?","The sum of its diagonal entries; it is also the sum of its eigenvalues counted with algebraic multiplicity."]
